# Plan Files

Plans live in `plans/` and are named `YYYY-MM-DD-short-slug.md`.

## Structure

```markdown
# Title (imperative, describes the outcome)

**Date:** YYYY-MM-DD
**Status:** Draft | Phase X in progress | Phase X done — awaiting sign-off | Complete
**Branch:** branch-name (if work happens off main)

## Description

What and why, in a few short paragraphs. Include key findings/constraints that
justify the approach, and a table of affected areas when useful.

## Steps

### Phase A — <name>
- [ ] Concrete, checkable step
- [ ] ...

### Phase A review gate — STOP for sign-off
- [ ] What the user should verify, as a checklist
- [ ] Decision: proceed / adjust / abandon

### Phase B — <name>
...

## Known limits / notes

Constraints, deferred items, risks, and follow-ups.
```

## Conventions

- Phases end in an explicit **review gate** whenever the next phase depends on
  user judgment (visual checks, trust decisions, deploys).
- Check off items (`[x]`) as they complete, in the same session they happen —
  annotate with brief results when useful (e.g. "7 pages written").
- Keep the **Status** line current; it's the single-glance state of the plan.
- Record decisions and discovered facts in the plan (e.g. "stray PDFs were never
  in git") so the plan stays the source of truth.
- Destructive or irreversible steps (deletes, deploys) belong in the final phase,
  after all sign-offs.
